            <ArticleTitle>Choledochal cyst and systemic lupus erythematosus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00383-010-2718-y</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 16-year-old female with systemic lupus erythematosus was diagnosed with choledochal cyst. As high-dose steroids had been prescribed for CNS lupus, surgery was performed under steroid cover. Despite postoperative pneumonia and wound infection, she is well 2 years later. There is no similar report in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
